        "problem": "$\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=$",
        "worked_solution": "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{2\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x+\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
